		transform: scale(1.03);
		filter: drop-shadow(0 10px 30px color-mix(in srgb, var(--bd-accent) 55%, transparent));
	}


	/* ═══ the closing tile on a phone ═════════════════════════════════
	   Kept at the end of the sheet on purpose: these override plain-class
	   rules written further down, and a media query carries no extra
	   specificity — only source order was ever going to settle it.
	   ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
	/* On a phone these two were stacking, which put the number below the
	   fold of the tile. They stay on one line: the button gives up its
	   padding, the number keeps its weight, and "or call us now" goes,
	   since a phone number beside a button needs no caption. */
	@media (max-width: 620px) {
